# SingVox Vercel upload exclusions.
# SCOPE: these rules are applied by the Vercel **CLI** when it uploads this directory as the
# deployment source. They are inert for a Git-connected deployment (the chosen method, plan 8.3):
# there, what is kept out of a deployment is what .gitignore keeps out of the repository, and the
# batch manifests under docs/migration/ are the authoritative record of that.
#
# Runtime requires ONLY:
#   public/avatar/SignVox_Female_Competition_Prototype.glb
#   public/spoter_pilot.onnx[.data], public/spoter_v2_model.onnx[.data]   (hosted externally, plan 5)
#   public/onnxruntime/*   (inference.ts pins /onnxruntime/ort-wasm-simd-threaded.wasm)
#
# The nine non-production GLBs below stay in the repository (history, experiments, fallback builds)
# but are referenced by no production path. All nine are gitignored and belong to no batch, so they
# are already absent from a Git-built deployment; they are listed here only so that an accidental
# CLI upload does not ship 464.7 MiB of unusable avatars.
#
# NOT listed, on purpose: public/avatar/test_front.png, test_side.png and test_hand.png (0.23 MiB).
# They are in Batch B and do ship in dist/avatar/. They were rendered by local Blender tooling
# (tools/test_neutral_pose.py and tools/render_hands.py write to a different output directory), and
# no application code, test or benchmark reads them, so they are left exactly as they are rather
# than added to this list.
public/avatar/SignVox_Female.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_backup.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_v2.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_v3.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_v5_HELLO.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_v4_HELLO.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_v4_Neutral.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_v5_Neutral.glb
public/avatar/SignVox_Female_v6_Neutral.glb
node_modules
dist
*.log
